    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\n\n- [X] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\n- [X] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\n- [X] I have updated 'mini.nvim' to latest version\n\n### Module(s)\n\nmini.sessions\n\n### Description\n\nThe default `mini.sessions`' path is incorrect in a way that at startup `mini.sessions` keeps erroring\r\n```\r\n(mini.sessions) \"C:\\\\\\\\Users\\\\\\\\B4mbus\\\\\\\\AppData\\\\\\\\Local\\\\\\\\nvim-data\\\\\\\\session\" is not a directory path\r\n```\r\nChanging it manually to `vim.fn.stdpath('data') .. '\\\\sessions\\\\` works and it doesn't display that error anymore.\r\n\r\nMy understanding is that on windows to create the directory one must append `\\\\` at the end. I'm willing to look into that, just creating that issue for organization purposes.\r\n\r\n(related to #133, but I'm splitting that issue into two)\n\n### Neovim version\n\n0.8.0-dev-922-g42e9fe7d9\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n1. `nvim -nu minimal.lua`\r\nContents of minimal.lua:\r\n```lua\r\nrequire('mini.sessions').setup({})\r\n```\n\n### Expected behavior\n\n`mini.session` properly creating, recognizing and using the default directory.\n\n### Actual behavior\n\n![image](https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/75364377/192996379-6c6b5fe3-b6e5-49d1-a991-7bffcfc19127.png)\r\n",
